__pycache__/
*.pyc
workspace/cloud/

site/.wrangler/
**/.wrangler/

# THE DAILY COPY OF THE INPUTS (20 September 2026, collection 274). bhs_update.py copies every file it is about to
# overwrite into live/backup_<date>. In a git repository that is a copy of what git already keeps: the previous version
# of each of those files is in the history of the commit that changed it. Committing the copies as well cost about 5 MB
# a day - one to two gigabytes a year - for nothing recoverable that is not recoverable without them.
data/105_bristow_hall_system_2026-09-08/live/backup_*

# v3.69 (22 September 2026, collection 302; the live-ops audit): no key file may be committed again (a local.env was committed on 18 September
# 2026 and deleted on 20 September; the keys are rotated by Anthony)
**/*.env
**/local.env

# audit-0924 (24 September 2026): the ETA 539 state panel is committed so the cloud keeps it current (s2/state539_live.py
# appends each week the Department publishes); the Department's 13 MB file and the backup copies it leaves beside the
# panel are not - they would add about 30 MB to the history every week.
data/37_dol_eta5159_2026-09/raw/
data/37_dol_eta5159_2026-09/panel/*.bak

